        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d965f64f-3d32-5cd6-a011-81fbcb803bab",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Huck Finn Jubilee\n- People: Ralph Stanley, Steve Martin, Rhonda Vincent, Carter Stanley\n- Bands: The String Cheese Incident, The Steep Canyon Rangers, The Stanley Brothers, The Clinch Mountain Boys\n- Topics: Bluegrass music\n\nFacts:\n- Ralph Stanley began playing music in 1946 with his brother Carter Stanley as part of The Stanley Brothers.\n- Ralph Stanley most often performed as the leader of his band The Clinch Mountain Boys.\n- Ralph Edmund Stanley was born on February 25, 1927, and he died on June 23, 2016.\n- Ralph Stanley, also known as Dr. Ralph Stanley, was an American bluegrass artist known for his distinctive singing and banjo playing.\n- Huck Finn Jubilee is the West Coast’s biggest bluegrass festival.\n- Huck Finn Jubilee has featured acts such as The String Cheese Incident, Ralph Stanley, Steve Martin & the Steep Canyon Rangers, and Rhonda Vincent.",
